                                        "sense_id": "a88c11e6-55ae-3ac8-8625-6f72a449b26f",
                                        "entry_id": "e70699a5-00d8-3414-a273-2f812b2415d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A young shoot of a plant; a spear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fbbc8c0-d1f2-481c-81bd-942f6a6b5884",
                                                "sense_id": "a88c11e6-55ae-3ac8-8625-6f72a449b26f",
                                                "text": "Clara had pulled a button from a hollyhock spire, and was breaking it to get the seeds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91d3a162-2585-300c-a4c2-533c2c217c80",
                                        "entry_id": "e70699a5-00d8-3414-a273-2f812b2415d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various tall grasses, rushes, or sedges, such as the marram, the reed canary-grass, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed48b068-ebc9-3bf7-87aa-615b9fcedebe",
                                        "entry_id": "e70699a5-00d8-3414-a273-2f812b2415d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sharp or tapering point."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33ef6088-568d-44c0-88df-518cf0ba324d",
                                                "sense_id": "ed48b068-ebc9-3bf7-87aa-615b9fcedebe",
                                                "text": "A beech wood with silver firs in it rolled down the face of the hill, and the maze of leafless twigs and dusky spires cut sharp against the soft blueness of the evening sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f59fb73-ce8f-4374-9483-c3268798d8b2",
                                                "sense_id": "ed48b068-ebc9-3bf7-87aa-615b9fcedebe",
                                                "text": "This park’s strange and beautiful rock formations were formed by the Yellowstone River and various streams that have cut through the rock over millions of years, carving out hoodoos, spires and caprocks. The name Makoshika comes from a Lakota word for badlands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cf48cca-2427-32ea-8974-35403aaba5ed",
                                        "entry_id": "e70699a5-00d8-3414-a273-2f812b2415d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tapering structure built on a roof or tower, especially as one of the central architectural features of a church or cathedral roof."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3f5bb8d-e315-458e-bb63-0c61daac6983",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf48cca-2427-32ea-8974-35403aaba5ed",
                                                "text": "The spire of the church rose high above the town."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6154821-8af4-3a76-988e-735583d66f90",
                                        "entry_id": "e70699a5-00d8-3414-a273-2f812b2415d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The top, or uppermost point, of anything; the summit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66da6bdb-9843-42df-94f8-0deff5036759",
                                                "sense_id": "f6154821-8af4-3a76-988e-735583d66f90",
                                                "text": "the spire and top of praises"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
